    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299-a1">

                <pb facs="0540" n="446" xml:id="pg446"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 393.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Lord
                            Iddesleigh</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 27,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of an instruction, under date of November 6, 1886, received by me from the
                    Secretary of State of the United States, relative to the case of the United
                    States fishing vessel the <hi rendition="#italic">Marion Grimes</hi>.</p>
                <p>The subject is so fully presented in this document, a copy of which I am
                    authorized by the Secretary to place in the hands of you lordship, that I can
                    add nothing to what is therein set forth, except to request your lordship’s
                    early attention to the case, which appears to be a very flagrant violation of
                    the rights secured to American fishermen under the treaty of 1818.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Phelps.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
